From: AxionOS <noreply@axionos>
Subject: [PATCH] camera2: take high speed fps ranges from a supported target

CameraConstrainedHighSpeedCaptureSessionImpl.createHighSpeedRequestList()
looks up the fps ranges with the size of
request.getTargets().iterator().next(). getTargets() is backed by an
ArraySet, so with a preview and a recording target the first one is
arbitrary. SurfaceUtils.checkConstrainedHighSpeedSurfaces() skips its
size check for privileged apps, so a privileged camera app can hand in
a recording surface that is larger than any advertised high speed size.
When that surface happens to come first,
StreamConfigurationMap.getHighSpeedVideoFpsRangesFor() throws:

    IllegalArgumentException: Size 3840x2160 does not support high speed video recording

and the recording never gets a repeating request (0 video samples,
MediaRecorder stop failed -1007). When the preview comes first the same
session records normally.

Use the size of a target that is an advertised high speed size, falling
back to the first target as before.
---
--- a/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraConstrainedHighSpeedCaptureSessionImpl.java
+++ b/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/impl/CameraConstrainedHighSpeedCaptureSessionImpl.java
@@ -102,8 +102,19 @@
 
         // Check the high speed video fps ranges for video size and find the min value from the list
         // and assign it to previewFps which will be used to calculate the requestList size.
-        Range<Integer>[] highSpeedFpsRanges = config.getHighSpeedVideoFpsRangesFor(
-                SurfaceUtils.getSurfaceSize(outputSurfaces.iterator().next()));
+        // Privileged apps skip the surface size check above, so a target can be larger than
+        // any advertised high speed size. getTargets() has no stable order: take the fps
+        // ranges from a target whose size is a high speed size instead of whichever is first.
+        List<Size> highSpeedSizes = Arrays.asList(config.getHighSpeedVideoSizes());
+        Size highSpeedSize = SurfaceUtils.getSurfaceSize(outputSurfaces.iterator().next());
+        for (Surface surface : outputSurfaces) {
+            Size surfaceSize = SurfaceUtils.getSurfaceSize(surface);
+            if (highSpeedSizes.contains(surfaceSize)) {
+                highSpeedSize = surfaceSize;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        Range<Integer>[] highSpeedFpsRanges = config.getHighSpeedVideoFpsRangesFor(highSpeedSize);
         Log.v(TAG, "High speed fps ranges: " + Arrays.toString(highSpeedFpsRanges));
         int previewFps = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
         for (Range<Integer> range : highSpeedFpsRanges) {
